# Docker Ignore Policy
.git/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.key
*.pem
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
**/.governance/vitest-results.json
**/.governance/coverage/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Python Tooling (not needed in container)
.coverage
# The xdist workers' own coverage data files (`.coverage.<host>.pid<n>.<rand>`),
# written beside `.coverage` by `make coverage-python` and left behind by an
# interrupted run. Excluded for the same reason `.coverage` above is, and with
# the same bounded effect: the only stage that copies anything copies `harness/`
# alone, so this keeps them out of the *build context*, not out of an image
# layer they could never have reached.
.coverage.*
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
# Wheels `pip download` / `pip wheel` leaves in the directory it ran from; six
# (mypy and its dependency closure, ~40 MB) sat in the repository root during
# the DEC-065 work. Same bounded effect as `.coverage.*` above -- context size,
# not image contents -- which is why this sits with the other root transients
# rather than being argued as a supply-chain control.
*.whl
htmlcov/

# IDE & System
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# Mango & Agent Subsystem
.mango/

# Test suites whose fixtures carry credential-shaped literals. The runtime image
# runs the Nemotron CLI and needs none of them, but `COPY harness/ /app/harness/`
# put `harness/shared/tests/` -- which holds a `ghp_...`, an `AKIA...` and
# `nvapi-...` strings -- into the context and therefore into the published image.
# Those literals are allowlisted for the *scan*; the allowlist says nothing about
# what ships.
#
# `harness/node/tests/` is deliberately NOT excluded here: `tsconfig.json`
# includes `tests/**/*.ts` and the build stage runs `tsc --noEmit`, so dropping
# it from the context would not fail the build -- it would quietly typecheck
# less. It is removed in the runtime stage instead, where nothing reads it.
#
# `harness/shared/governance-policy.json` must NEVER be excluded: since the
# Nemotron policy wiring (R-TDH-13) `src/ai/nemotron/policy.ts` reads it at
# module load and throws on absence, so the image's own CMD (`cli.ts`) fails to
# start without it. The runtime is Node-only, but it is not Python-free.
harness/shared/tests/
harness/api_server/tests/
harness/control-plane/tests/
harness/jvm/src/test/

# Build & Scratch Artifacts
.gradle/
**/.gradle/
scratch/
.benchmarks/
coverage.json
*_history.json
*_history_pretty.json
*_loop_dump.json

# Editable install metadata (pip install -e .)
*.egg-info/
mango_code_agent_harness.egg-info/

# Pytest / Hypothesis temp directories created during local runs
harness/node/test-*/
.hypothesis/

# Agent session state (never a build input); .mango/ above already covers the memory store
.claude/

# IDE tooling — not needed in the container image
pyrightconfig.json
